What changed (a VR fork of Hookshot)
------------------------------------

HookshotVR is a modified version of Hookshot (https://git.notrexed.dev/Hookshot/Hookshot), the static recompilation of
the game by NotRexed and its contributors. It was made from Hookshot's source in November 2026. Hookshot's own code is
still here, in its own folders, so its updates can be merged.

What this fork adds or changes:

  - vr/: everything for VR. The OpenXR session and the headset's frames; both eyes ("From depth" and "True stereo");
    the head-driven camera; Link's body, hands and held items; sword, shield, bombs, bottles, bow, slingshot, boomerang,
    hookshot, ocarina and the other items in the hands; the wrist HUD, the radial wheel and the VR menu; comfort options;
    the Window view; cutscenes and Item Get views for VR.
  - vr/launcher/: the HookshotVR Launcher, which builds the game with Hookshot's builder and starts it.
  - assets/vr/: the art of the VR menu.
  - Small changes ("VR HOOK" markers) in Hookshot's own files, so the renderer and the game can talk to the VR code.

Every change is in this repository's history and marked in the files that were changed.


Third-party parts we add
------------------------

  EB Garamond (the launcher's font)
    The EB Garamond Project Authors. SIL Open Font License 1.1.
    Files: vr/launcher/fonts/ (licence: vr/launcher/fonts/OFL.txt; where it came from: PROVENANCE.md there).

  OpenXR headers
    The Khronos Group Inc. Apache-2.0 or MIT.
    Files: vr/third_party/openxr/.

  OpenXR loader (openxr_loader.dll on Windows; on Linux libopenxr_loader.so.1)
    The Khronos Group Inc. Apache-2.0 (https://github.com/KhronosGroup/OpenXR-SDK).
    Loaded at run time, so the launcher and the game can find your VR runtime. The Windows download carries it beside
    the launcher, unchanged; on Linux it is your system's.

  Dear ImGui (the launcher's interface)
    Omar Cornut and contributors. MIT.
    Files: third_party/imgui/ (licence: LICENSE.txt there).

  SDL2 (windows and controllers, loaded at run time)
    Sam Lantinga and contributors. zlib licence.
    Files: third_party/sdl2/ (licence: LICENSE.txt there).

  libpng (the launcher's pictures, when it is built with it)
    The PNG Reference Library Authors. libpng licence.

The parts Hookshot itself carries (Eden and suyu code, Sirit, the Vulkan Memory Allocator, Opus, zstd, zbic, the
Libertinus fonts, AMD FidelityFX and the others) keep their own notices in their folders, as Hookshot lists in
docs/hookshot-readme.md ("License" and "Credits"). Hookshot's builder, which the release bundles at the version we build on, brings its
own parts with their licence notices, inside its folder.

The leather and copper frame (assets/vr/panel_frame.png) and the launcher's frame and wordmark are the project's own art.


